=============== WIRES TO BE USED WITH THE REST OF THE PROJECT =======================

mouse:
wire left_click: 1 if left mouse button was clicked, 0 otherwise
wire right_click: 1 if right mouse button was clicked, 0 otherwise
wire middle_click: 1 if middle mouse button was clicked, 0 otherwise

wire [9:0] x_position: 10 bit value holding current x position on the VGA display
wire [9:0] y_position: 10 bit value holding current y position on the VGA display

ex. if (x_position == 10'd320) and (y_position == 10'd240), then you are in the MIDDLE 
of the VGA display (640x480 pixel resolution)

keyboard:
wire [7:0] key_pressed: 8 bit hexadecimal value holding the character code of the key key_pressed

ex. if (key_pressed == 8'h1E), then TOOL should be ERASE 

IMPORTANT:
SW[9] = 1 --> MOUSE MODE
SW[9] = 0 --> KEYBOARD MODE

========== KEYBOARD TO HOST CODES ==============

TOOLS SWITCHING

KEY - TOOL - HEXCODE - BINARY
1 - BRUSH - 16 - 010110
2 - ERASE - 1E - 011110
3 - LINE - 26 - 100110
4 - PAINT BUCKET - 25 - 100101

COLOURS SWITCHING - NUMPAD

KEY - COLOUR - HEXCODE - BINARY
1 - BLACK - 69 - 1101001
2 - RED - 72 - 1110010
3 - BLUE - 7A - 1111010
4 - GREEN - 6B - 1101011
5 - WHITE - 73 - 1110011

PEN SIZE 

ARROWUP - INCREASE SIZE - 55 - 1010101
ARROWDOWN - DECREASE SIZE - 4E - 1001110




=========== HOST TO KEYBOARD COMMAND ===========
FA = ACK (acknowledge) (keyboard to host)

HEXCODE --------------- FUNCTIONALITY
F4                      Keyboard Enable: clears output buffer, enables keyboard, returns ACK
                                        keycodes will be transmitted !!
F5                      Keyboard Disable: resets keyboard, disables keyboard, returns ACK
                                        keycodes will NOT be transmitted !!

